      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "(BY SRI. R.D. RENUKARADHYA, HCGP FOR R1)\n -2-  CRL.P No. 213 of 2023  THIS CRIMINAL PETITION FILED UNDER SECTION 482 OF CR.P.C. PRAYING TO QUASH THE FIR AND COMPLAINT IN CR.NO.270/2022 DATED 08.11.2022 FOR THE OFFENCES PUNISHABLE UNDER SECTIONS 498A, 34 OF IPC AND SECTIONS 3, 4 OF D.P ACT REGISTERED BY THE 1st RESPONDENT POLICE VIDE ANNEXURE-A AND A1 IN ANNAPOORNESHWARI NAGAR POLICE STATION ON THE FILE OF THE V ACMM, BANGALORE.\n THIS PETITION, COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS DAY, THE COURT MADE THE FOLLOWING:\n ORDER Learned High Court Government Pleader accepts notice for respondent No.1 - State and submits that the Police have already investigated the matter and filed the charge-sheet.\n2. At this stage, learned counsel for the petitioners seeks permission of this Court to withdraw the petition with liberty to file fresh petition challenging the charge-sheet.\n3. Submission of learned counsel is placed on record.",
